{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
WHAT LIES AT THE END OF THE MELON PATCH

26
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:38,025
- [indistinct chatter]
- [Legoshi pants]

27
00:01:40,986 --> 00:01:41,987
[grunts softly]

28
00:01:45,616 --> 00:01:46,450
Huh?

29
00:01:46,534 --> 00:01:47,660
[upbeat music playing]

30
00:01:47,743 --> 00:01:49,745
[indistinct chatter]

31
00:01:49,829 --> 00:01:50,913
MEAT EATERS FEST

32
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:53,082
<i>What's going on?</i>

33
00:01:53,165 --> 00:01:55,459
OPENING SALE

34
00:01:55,543 --> 00:01:56,669
<i>Everyone's so...</i>

35
00:01:57,294 --> 00:01:58,129
<i>happy.</i>

36
00:01:59,547 --> 00:02:02,800
CONGRATULATIONS!
OPENING SALE

37
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:05,094
Excuse me.

38
00:02:05,553 --> 00:02:08,305
Udon? I didn't order any udon today.

39
00:02:08,389 --> 00:02:12,434
Oh, no, I'm not here for that. I was just...
Is this a festival or something?

40
00:02:12,977 --> 00:02:15,813
You must be the only carnivore in town
who hasn't heard.

41
00:02:15,896 --> 00:02:17,481
Heard what?

42
00:02:17,565 --> 00:02:19,900
- Here we are. Take a look.
- Huh?

43
00:02:20,401 --> 00:02:21,527
YAHYA IS DEAD!

44
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:23,112
- [gasps] Mr. Yahya!
- What?

45
00:02:23,195 --> 00:02:26,490
It almost sounds
as if you liked the old nag.

46
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,534
Huh?

47
00:02:29,201 --> 00:02:32,163
{\an8}With him gone, we can sell meat
without fear of retribution,

48
00:02:32,246 --> 00:02:33,914
which has everyone in a great mood.

49
00:02:33,998 --> 00:02:37,751
This place is brimming with customers who
don't have to worry about getting caught.

50
00:02:37,835 --> 00:02:41,213
But do we actually know
that Mr. Yahya is dead?

51
00:02:41,755 --> 00:02:44,884
I suppose we don't.
Somebody could be pulling a prank.

52
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:47,094
He doesn't seem like he'd be easy to kill.

53
00:02:47,177 --> 00:02:49,972
[chuckles nervously] That's for sure.
He knows how to take a punch.

54
00:02:50,055 --> 00:02:53,601
Well, now! You've really been
in a fight with Yahya?

55
00:02:53,684 --> 00:02:56,937
Huh? [chuckles nervously] Well...

56
00:02:57,021 --> 00:03:00,983
Wow! That scar on your face
ain't just for show, huh?

57
00:03:01,483 --> 00:03:03,319
But even so, people have been saying

58
00:03:03,402 --> 00:03:06,113
that Yahya's been losing his touch
in his old age.

59
00:03:06,655 --> 00:03:08,908
It's possible someone really did off him.

60
00:03:09,909 --> 00:03:12,870
[Legoshi] <i>I didn't like the way
Mr. Yahya did things either.</i>

61
00:03:13,704 --> 00:03:17,708
<i>I can understand why the carnivores
are celebrating and all, but, still...</i>

62
00:03:17,791 --> 00:03:20,544
[seller] Young man, don't you have
a delivery to get to?

63
00:03:20,628 --> 00:03:22,379
[gasps] Oh, you're right!

64
00:03:22,963 --> 00:03:23,797
Bye!

65
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:30,012
[siren wailing in distance]

66
00:03:35,267 --> 00:03:37,394
[horns honking]

67
00:03:46,111 --> 00:03:47,696
[paper rustling]

68
00:03:48,739 --> 00:03:51,992
These flyers are being posted
all over the Black Market.

69
00:03:52,576 --> 00:03:55,037
We're pretty sure
it's the work of that counselor.

70
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:57,081
Been looking everywhere for that guy, but...

71
00:03:57,164 --> 00:03:59,625
[clicks tongue, inhales] so far, nothing.

72
00:04:00,292 --> 00:04:04,129
[Yahya] <i>Damn him.
He clearly knows that I'm still alive.</i>

73
00:04:05,172 --> 00:04:06,632
<i>So, what's he up to?</i>

74
00:04:07,841 --> 00:04:10,552
Maybe he tried escaping
into the Black Market.

75
00:04:10,636 --> 00:04:13,597
Although, why would an herbivore
go to a place like that?

76
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:17,643
[Melon] <i>The name's Melon. Remember it.</i>

77
00:04:18,602 --> 00:04:22,064
No, Corne, search the Black Market
from top to bottom.

78
00:04:22,147 --> 00:04:23,774
Huh? You mean it?

79
00:04:23,857 --> 00:04:26,318
Our suspect, his name is Melon.

80
00:04:26,944 --> 00:04:29,905
He may have the face of a gazelle,
but do not be deceived.

81
00:04:30,531 --> 00:04:32,992
He also has
the deadly fangs of a carnivore.

82
00:04:33,075 --> 00:04:36,287
- What?
- Melon's mixed, the son of a bitch.

83
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:37,538
He's mixed?

84
00:04:38,038 --> 00:04:40,708
Then that means,
he'll have hunting instincts too.

85
00:04:40,791 --> 00:04:42,459
[grunts in frustration] He had me fooled!

86
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,005
All right, I'll refocus the investigation.

87
00:04:46,088 --> 00:04:47,172
I swear, what a pain.

88
00:04:47,256 --> 00:04:50,592
Mixed? You think you got a nose
for these kinds of things.

89
00:04:50,676 --> 00:04:53,971
[Yahya] <i>You were deliberately
trying to show me your face.</i>

90
00:04:54,054 --> 00:04:57,599
[Melon] <i>Ah, we finally get to meet.</i>
[inhales sharply]

91
00:04:57,683 --> 00:05:00,436
<i>But now I can't invite you to the party.
What a shame.</i>

92
00:05:01,937 --> 00:05:04,189
[Yahya] <i>Does he actually want me
at the party?</i>

93
00:05:05,399 --> 00:05:06,525
<i>Hmm.</i>

94
00:05:06,608 --> 00:05:10,654
<i>Now that I know the truth about you,
was that a challenge?</i>

95
00:05:11,697 --> 00:05:12,740
[thuds]

96
00:05:13,532 --> 00:05:14,867
<i>Or was it a threat?</i>

97
00:05:16,618 --> 00:05:17,828
<i>Melon...</i>

98
00:05:19,121 --> 00:05:20,748
<i>I will find you,</i>

99
00:05:21,415 --> 00:05:24,626
<i>and I'll use you as fertilizer
for my carrots.</i>

100
00:05:25,544 --> 00:05:27,546
[whirring]

101
00:05:28,505 --> 00:05:32,342
UDON BEBEBE

102
00:05:32,426 --> 00:05:34,470
[anchor] <i>The first trial has been held</i>

103
00:05:34,553 --> 00:05:36,805
<i>in the Madara-Gumi
drug manufacturing case,</i>

104
00:05:36,889 --> 00:05:37,806
<i>which was exposed...</i>

105
00:05:37,890 --> 00:05:40,768
[Legoshi] <i>People were going wild
in the Black Market,</i>

106
00:05:40,851 --> 00:05:45,105
<i>but they're not reporting
on Mr. Yahya in the news at all.</i>

107
00:05:45,773 --> 00:05:49,485
<i>Hmm. Well, maybe this is something
I shouldn't worry about.</i>

108
00:05:49,568 --> 00:05:51,236
[anchor] <i>Now for our next item.</i>

109
00:05:51,862 --> 00:05:55,240
<i>According to the city's
Co-Existence and Co-Prosperity Committee,</i>

110
00:05:55,324 --> 00:05:57,618
<i>it has been decided that,
starting this month,</i>

111
00:05:57,701 --> 00:06:01,914
<i>households of families with mixed children
will receive subsidies from the city.</i>

112
00:06:02,956 --> 00:06:06,043
<i>This initiative is called
the "Live Together Support Fund."</i>

113
00:06:06,126 --> 00:06:08,754
<i>It has been created
to financially support families</i>

114
00:06:08,837 --> 00:06:10,881
<i>born from inter-species marriages,</i>

115
00:06:10,964 --> 00:06:15,260
<i>which, while legally recognized,
continue to face societal discrimination.</i>

116
00:06:15,344 --> 00:06:18,597
[Legoshi] <i>Hmm. I had no idea
things like that even existed.</i>

117
00:06:19,681 --> 00:06:21,517
- [zebra] Give me a break!
- Huh?

118
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:22,851
Why should I pay my taxes

119
00:06:22,935 --> 00:06:25,604
when they want to waste them
on this kind of nonsense?

120
00:06:25,687 --> 00:06:28,857
They can dress it up by calling it
interspecies-romance,

121
00:06:28,941 --> 00:06:31,527
but it's just young folks
rushing into things without thinking,

122
00:06:31,610 --> 00:06:33,946
and then popping out some messed up kids!

123
00:06:34,029 --> 00:06:37,032
They're just setting themselves up
for discrimination. Right?

124
00:06:37,533 --> 00:06:39,493
Oh, uh... [laughs nervously]

125
00:06:40,035 --> 00:06:41,286
- More noodles!
- Yes, sir!

126
00:06:42,121 --> 00:06:42,955
Huh.

127
00:06:43,747 --> 00:06:46,250
- [Legoshi] Another batch of noodles.
- Coming up.

128
00:06:47,584 --> 00:06:52,047
And, hey, don't pay him any mind.
All kinds of species come into this place.

129
00:06:52,714 --> 00:06:54,800
Thanks. Really, I'm fine.

130
00:06:55,425 --> 00:06:58,053
You know, you've become quite the waiter.

131
00:06:58,137 --> 00:06:59,304
Wait, do you mean that?

132
00:06:59,388 --> 00:07:01,682
Yep. I admit you had me worried
at first, though.

133
00:07:01,765 --> 00:07:04,977
You shook like a leaf on a tree
every time you had to serve an herbivore.

134
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:07,646
[chuckles nervously] Well, you know,
that's because I, uh...

135
00:07:07,729 --> 00:07:08,856
[pleasant music playing]

136
00:07:08,939 --> 00:07:10,274
No, I get it.

137
00:07:10,357 --> 00:07:12,484
Don't forget, I'm a carnivore.

138
00:07:12,568 --> 00:07:16,363
When I first opened this place,
I didn't have one herbivore customer.

139
00:07:16,447 --> 00:07:17,906
None of them ate here?

140
00:07:17,990 --> 00:07:20,742
So, then, what was it that finally
brought them all in?

141
00:07:20,826 --> 00:07:22,202
[Sunaga] Hmm.

142
00:07:22,286 --> 00:07:24,288
This stuff here. The udon.

143
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:28,542
Herbivores who only ordered delivery
would eventually come in,

144
00:07:28,625 --> 00:07:30,502
saying they had to try it
fresh from the pot.

145
00:07:31,086 --> 00:07:33,380
Well, I guess that's the magic
of good food.

146
00:07:34,423 --> 00:07:37,843
[Sunaga] I don't know much about this
"Live it, gather fund," or whatever it is,

147
00:07:38,552 --> 00:07:41,180
but I do know that
if people eat good stuff together,

148
00:07:41,263 --> 00:07:43,432
then that's enough
to make anyone happy. Isn't it?

149
00:07:44,516 --> 00:07:46,935
I think that you might be right.

150
00:07:47,936 --> 00:07:50,022
- Okay, quit dawdling.
- Huh?

151
00:07:50,564 --> 00:07:52,483
The customer, he's still waiting.

152
00:07:52,566 --> 00:07:53,775
Uh... Right.

153
00:08:06,914 --> 00:08:09,583
[mellow piano music playing]

154
00:08:12,753 --> 00:08:13,712
When I was little,

155
00:08:14,671 --> 00:08:17,049
we had a wooden table
in our kitchen, didn't we?

156
00:08:17,799 --> 00:08:18,967
You remember that, Mom?

157
00:08:20,135 --> 00:08:23,096
I always liked that table.

158
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:27,142
Or at least I liked eating around it,
with you and Grandpa. That was the best.

159
00:08:28,393 --> 00:08:32,481
And somewhere deep down, I always wanted
a family of my own like that.

160
00:08:34,191 --> 00:08:36,777
By the way, I'm seeing someone.

161
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:40,405
Now don't be surprised,
but she's a dwarf rabbit.

162
00:08:40,489 --> 00:08:41,865
[Gosha] A dwarf rabbit?

163
00:08:42,991 --> 00:08:44,326
Grandpa?

164
00:08:44,910 --> 00:08:47,746
Uh, sorry about that.
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

165
00:08:48,747 --> 00:08:50,332
But did I hear that right?

166
00:08:50,415 --> 00:08:53,418
Are you seriously dating a rabbit?

167
00:08:53,502 --> 00:08:57,798
Yeah. To be perfectly honest,
I'm hoping to marry her someday.

168
00:08:57,881 --> 00:08:59,466
No kidding.

169
00:08:59,550 --> 00:09:02,302
It's not easy for inter-species families
to get by,

170
00:09:02,386 --> 00:09:04,721
but, obviously, you know that already.

171
00:09:04,805 --> 00:09:06,807
When one's a carnivore
and one's an herbivore--

172
00:09:06,890 --> 00:09:08,517
I've made my peace with that.

173
00:09:09,851 --> 00:09:11,436
I'm serious here.

174
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:14,106
I've given it a lot of thought.
I've trained for it.

175
00:09:14,898 --> 00:09:19,069
Didn't I tell you? I'm not the...
the kid you once knew.

176
00:09:19,152 --> 00:09:21,488
[sighs] That's right.

177
00:09:22,322 --> 00:09:23,574
I guess you're not.

178
00:09:23,657 --> 00:09:26,034
You've grown into a hell of a young man.

179
00:09:28,328 --> 00:09:31,957
All her life, your mother had to carry
the pain of being mixed,

180
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:34,835
and I was never able
to confront the issue.

181
00:09:34,918 --> 00:09:35,919
Why is that?

182
00:09:37,212 --> 00:09:38,338
I was afraid.

183
00:09:39,131 --> 00:09:42,092
I never had the guts
to actually address the subject.

184
00:09:42,175 --> 00:09:45,220
But you, you got a lot more backbone.

185
00:09:46,013 --> 00:09:49,099
You're the sort of kid
who can bring someone flowers.

186
00:09:50,726 --> 00:09:52,060
If anyone can do it...

187
00:09:53,812 --> 00:09:55,522
That means a lot. Thanks, Grandpa.

188
00:09:56,106 --> 00:09:58,191
[Gosha] Yeah,
but you're still getting one of these!

189
00:09:58,275 --> 00:10:00,110
[Legoshi laughing] Ow, that's hurts!

190
00:10:00,193 --> 00:10:01,987
- Cut it out!
- [both laughing]

191
00:10:05,657 --> 00:10:08,410
[doctor] You're here
to sell your shell today, correct?

192
00:10:08,493 --> 00:10:09,578
[whirring]

193
00:10:09,661 --> 00:10:12,039
As part of our
"Yahya Death Memorial Campaign,"

194
00:10:12,122 --> 00:10:13,957
we will be skipping the anesthesia!

195
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:16,793
Whoa, whoa, wait.
Who'd you say this campaign's for?

196
00:10:16,877 --> 00:10:20,297
Fear has a way of making a shell shrink
and zip up nutrients.

197
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,841
And a healthy shell
is what we pay generously for.

198
00:10:22,924 --> 00:10:25,302
- That's the campaign in a nutshell.
- [yelps]

199
00:10:25,385 --> 00:10:27,596
I'll take the anesthesia,
and the low price!

200
00:10:27,679 --> 00:10:29,681
[whirring continues]

201
00:10:30,724 --> 00:10:33,935
[doctor] Excuse me! You can't just
barge into the operating room!

202
00:10:35,187 --> 00:10:37,272
- [machine whirring]
- [wheelchair rattling]

203
00:10:39,316 --> 00:10:40,233
Yahya...

204
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,986
- [gasping]
- You're not dead.

205
00:10:43,070 --> 00:10:43,904
[Yahya] Nope.

206
00:10:44,946 --> 00:10:46,907
It seems your campaign
will have to be delayed.

207
00:10:48,533 --> 00:10:49,576
[whirring stops]

208
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:51,662
What brings you here this fine day?

209
00:10:51,745 --> 00:10:54,665
We practice nothing but
the most legitimate medical procedures

210
00:10:54,748 --> 00:10:57,000
- at this facility--
- Spare me the sales pitch.

211
00:10:57,084 --> 00:10:58,418
I don't have time for it.

212
00:10:58,919 --> 00:11:01,004
Just tell me what I want to know.

213
00:11:01,088 --> 00:11:03,215
You're using ivory in your Hyperdrug.

214
00:11:03,298 --> 00:11:05,967
Where and from whom
were you receiving your supply?

215
00:11:06,051 --> 00:11:07,719
Sorry, that's a trade secret.

216
00:11:10,555 --> 00:11:11,515
[doctor yelps]

217
00:11:12,224 --> 00:11:13,892
My patience is very thin.

218
00:11:13,975 --> 00:11:16,061
Stop! Please! [whimpering]

219
00:11:16,144 --> 00:11:18,105
I suggest that you answer me now.

220
00:11:18,939 --> 00:11:21,900
Unless you'd like to examine
the bottom of my shoe up close.

221
00:11:22,526 --> 00:11:24,111
From a gazelle! A gazelle!

222
00:11:24,194 --> 00:11:26,196
That crazy herbivore
showed up out of nowhere

223
00:11:26,279 --> 00:11:27,614
with a big stash of ivory.

224
00:11:27,697 --> 00:11:28,824
[Corne] You sure about that?

225
00:11:28,907 --> 00:11:31,118
He was wearing a mask
so I couldn't see his face,

226
00:11:31,201 --> 00:11:32,953
but there's no mistaking horns like that.

227
00:11:33,036 --> 00:11:36,289
So, right when you needed ivory,
this mysterious gazelle appeared?

228
00:11:36,373 --> 00:11:40,293
Yeah. The original plan was for us
to get it from the Shishi-Gumi,

229
00:11:40,377 --> 00:11:42,504
but this gazelle showed up with the ivory,

230
00:11:42,587 --> 00:11:45,966
and even demanded that the Shishi-Gumi
make him their new boss.

231
00:11:46,049 --> 00:11:48,135
[yelps] Don't tell anybody I told you!

232
00:11:48,218 --> 00:11:50,387
This can't get back to me! I beg you!

233
00:11:51,179 --> 00:11:53,765
Hey, give me the anesthesia!
I won't tell a soul!

234
00:11:55,308 --> 00:11:56,643
{\an8}[mysterious music playing]

235
00:11:58,812 --> 00:12:01,356
[Chloe] Here. The report you requested.

236
00:12:02,065 --> 00:12:03,316
[Louis] I appreciate it.

237
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,068
[Chloe scoffs] So you should.

238
00:12:05,652 --> 00:12:07,946
Unlike you students, I'm actually busy.

239
00:12:08,613 --> 00:12:09,698
Anything of note?

240
00:12:11,158 --> 00:12:12,075
[inhales]

241
00:12:12,993 --> 00:12:14,411
[exhales]

242
00:12:14,494 --> 00:12:17,747
In short, it's just your ordinary,
run-of-the-mill energy drink,

243
00:12:18,206 --> 00:12:20,500
but with several unusual ingredients.

244
00:12:20,584 --> 00:12:21,626
Unusual?

245
00:12:21,710 --> 00:12:24,337
Just things that normally
wouldn't be detectable.

246
00:12:24,421 --> 00:12:26,882
As to how they got in there, though,
who's to say.

247
00:12:27,424 --> 00:12:28,842
I look forward to giving it a read.

248
00:12:29,634 --> 00:12:31,845
I'm can't say I'm sure what you're up to,

249
00:12:31,928 --> 00:12:34,139
but tell me if you find
anything interesting.

250
00:12:34,723 --> 00:12:36,057
Maybe I will.

251
00:12:36,141 --> 00:12:39,811
But there's a chance it'll be something
you wish you didn't know. [sneers]

252
00:12:41,688 --> 00:12:45,108
- [Noris snoring]
- [hurried footsteps approaching]

253
00:12:50,489 --> 00:12:53,700
Hey, rise and shine.
It's time for your shift.

254
00:12:53,783 --> 00:12:56,077
[sighing] Huh? Yeah.

255
00:12:56,995 --> 00:12:59,414
[groaning]

256
00:12:59,498 --> 00:13:01,333
Well, how are things looking?

257
00:13:01,416 --> 00:13:03,210
No movement so far.

258
00:13:03,293 --> 00:13:05,378
Just a lot of playing cards and drinking.

259
00:13:05,462 --> 00:13:08,465
[sighs] I guess Melon isn't coming back.

260
00:13:08,548 --> 00:13:10,091
- [engine starts]
- Huh?

261
00:13:10,175 --> 00:13:11,343
[both grunt]

262
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:16,348
[mouse] Wait, Noris!

263
00:13:16,431 --> 00:13:18,600
- [thudding]
- Huh?

264
00:13:18,683 --> 00:13:21,853
Hey, you're driving.
Keep your damn eyes on the road.

265
00:13:21,937 --> 00:13:23,855
Didn't you hear some kind of noise?

266
00:13:23,939 --> 00:13:26,525
- Like what?
- Eh, forget about it.

267
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:30,028
[straining]

268
00:13:40,038 --> 00:13:42,040
[squeaking]

269
00:13:42,123 --> 00:13:43,959
[ominous classical music playing]

270
00:13:46,002 --> 00:13:47,921
All right, what's the big idea

271
00:13:48,004 --> 00:13:49,756
calling us here
in the middle of the night?

272
00:13:49,839 --> 00:13:52,759
The product is ready, so I contacted you.

273
00:13:52,842 --> 00:13:55,136
And here it is. Isn't it beautiful?

274
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:57,639
It wasn't easy to prepare
this much deer dung,

275
00:13:57,722 --> 00:14:00,225
but it's plain to see
it was worth the effort.

276
00:14:00,308 --> 00:14:03,895
All this manure and poop stuff
really turns you on, huh?

277
00:14:03,979 --> 00:14:06,815
You say that, but you guys
are the ones buying it, right?

278
00:14:09,067 --> 00:14:11,027
Wait, hold on. Is this all?

279
00:14:11,111 --> 00:14:12,737
[Deshico] Yep. That's all of it.

280
00:14:12,821 --> 00:14:15,448
[Free snarls] Are you kidding?
That's nowhere near enough.

281
00:14:15,532 --> 00:14:17,033
This is a high-quality product

282
00:14:17,117 --> 00:14:19,369
and a different class
from the likes of Kines.

283
00:14:19,452 --> 00:14:22,372
That means there's a limit to how much
we can produce per delivery.

284
00:14:22,455 --> 00:14:24,541
That wasn't the agreement and you know it!

285
00:14:24,624 --> 00:14:26,960
Trying to scare me
will not get you more dung.

286
00:14:27,043 --> 00:14:28,628
It's a difficult formulation.

287
00:14:29,212 --> 00:14:32,299
But because of that,
I am fully confident in its quality.

288
00:14:32,382 --> 00:14:33,300
But still!

289
00:14:33,383 --> 00:14:36,720
And, if something is rare,
it simply becomes more desirable.

290
00:14:36,803 --> 00:14:40,015
My product here will make your boss
an overnight celebrity.

291
00:14:41,349 --> 00:14:43,685
And now, would you kindly
sign the receipt?

292
00:14:45,604 --> 00:14:47,981
It's so perfect,
I almost hate to let it all go.

293
00:14:48,064 --> 00:14:48,899
[pen rasping]

294
00:14:48,982 --> 00:14:52,736
Rare is the thing that can bring happiness
to both carnivores and herbivores.

295
00:14:52,819 --> 00:14:55,155
But everyone
is going to love it, I'm sure.

296
00:14:55,238 --> 00:14:57,073
- Like they love me.
- [Free] Shut up!

297
00:14:57,157 --> 00:15:00,035
Next time, you'll give us
the amount we agreed on!

298
00:15:00,619 --> 00:15:03,663
Then I take it, you'll be on poop duty
for the next delivery?

299
00:15:03,747 --> 00:15:05,790
You better hope I'm not! [snarls]

300
00:15:09,544 --> 00:15:10,545
[door opens]

301
00:15:10,629 --> 00:15:12,464
[footsteps receding]

302
00:15:12,547 --> 00:15:13,381
[door closes]

303
00:15:19,512 --> 00:15:21,014
[sniffing]

304
00:15:21,097 --> 00:15:23,475
Oh, man, what is it now?

305
00:15:23,558 --> 00:15:26,186
Doesn't it smell like
a sewer or something in here?

306
00:15:26,269 --> 00:15:28,313
If you're smelling a sewer,
it's probably your mane.

307
00:15:28,396 --> 00:15:29,439
Lay off, would ya?

308
00:15:29,522 --> 00:15:30,690
[suspenseful music playing]

309
00:15:30,774 --> 00:15:32,484
Maybe I'm just...

310
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:34,152
Hey! Watch the road!

311
00:15:34,235 --> 00:15:36,613
- [horn blaring]
- [tires screech]

312
00:15:37,197 --> 00:15:39,699
That's exactly why I said
not to take your eyes off the road!

313
00:15:39,783 --> 00:15:41,618
[Agata] I'm sorry! I'll be careful!

314
00:15:41,701 --> 00:15:44,996
- [Free] I'm surrounded by idiots!
- I'll keep my eyes forward!

315
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,540
- [Free] Better! Or you're going to pay!
- Yes, sir!

316
00:15:47,624 --> 00:15:48,458
Huh?

317
00:15:50,126 --> 00:15:51,419
[softly] Oh.

318
00:15:52,712 --> 00:15:54,089
What is this?

319
00:15:59,427 --> 00:16:01,096
So, uh, where do we put all this?

320
00:16:01,179 --> 00:16:03,390
On the bar counter
should probably be fine.

321
00:16:03,473 --> 00:16:04,307
Got it.

322
00:16:05,183 --> 00:16:06,351
[Agata grunts]

323
00:16:08,979 --> 00:16:10,522
[Free] You got to wonder...

324
00:16:11,106 --> 00:16:14,067
This stuff, after all our help getting it,

325
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:16,528
do you think we might get to try
a bit of it?

326
00:16:16,611 --> 00:16:18,029
Yeah, I doubt it.

327
00:16:18,655 --> 00:16:21,282
- It's supposed to be super expensive.
- Right.

328
00:16:21,366 --> 00:16:24,995
The boss said he's unveiling it
personally at the Masquerade Night Party,

329
00:16:25,078 --> 00:16:26,287
so it's going to be big.

330
00:16:26,371 --> 00:16:27,706
Unusual, though, huh?

331
00:16:27,789 --> 00:16:29,916
He basically never shows himself
in public.

332
00:16:30,625 --> 00:16:32,877
There. So, are we all finished here?

333
00:16:32,961 --> 00:16:34,921
Sure. Think we're squared away.

334
00:16:36,006 --> 00:16:36,965
[sighs]

335
00:16:37,716 --> 00:16:40,593
I wonder how much sleep
I'm actually going to get tonight.

336
00:16:40,677 --> 00:16:42,929
Bet we'll have more prep to do
in the morning.

337
00:16:43,013 --> 00:16:44,139
This sucks.

338
00:16:44,848 --> 00:16:45,932
[thudding]

339
00:16:46,683 --> 00:16:49,144
I knew I heard someone rummaging around!

340
00:16:49,227 --> 00:16:50,854
So here's where you were hiding!

341
00:16:52,731 --> 00:16:53,606
Huh?

342
00:16:53,690 --> 00:16:56,192
You idiot, there's nothing in there.

343
00:16:56,276 --> 00:16:58,820
Why are you jumping
at every shadow you see, huh?

344
00:16:58,903 --> 00:17:00,238
You're a lion, ain't ya?

345
00:17:00,321 --> 00:17:03,700
- About time you start acting like one!
- [Agata] Yeah, you're right.

346
00:17:04,701 --> 00:17:07,912
Clearly, something's off with me today.
Any chance you can drive?

347
00:17:07,996 --> 00:17:09,372
- [Free] Hell no!
- Oh, man.

348
00:17:10,373 --> 00:17:11,207
[switch clicks]

349
00:17:15,170 --> 00:17:16,171
[exhales softly]

350
00:17:17,255 --> 00:17:18,089
[grunts]

351
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:24,471
INVITATION
MASQUERADE PARTY

352
00:17:24,554 --> 00:17:26,598
[Noris over call] <i>The Shishi-Gumi
plan on hosting</i>

353
00:17:26,681 --> 00:17:29,225
<i>a Masquerade Night Party
per the invitation.</i>

354
00:17:30,685 --> 00:17:32,353
That explains things.

355
00:17:33,146 --> 00:17:35,440
This has to be the party
he was talking about.

356
00:17:36,608 --> 00:17:38,526
Well, this is going to be fun.

357
00:17:38,610 --> 00:17:40,695
I'll go and prepare our reinforcements.

358
00:17:40,779 --> 00:17:44,616
No. I have to settle things
with him personally.

359
00:17:44,699 --> 00:17:47,911
You're kidding! Do you really think
that you could do this alone?

360
00:17:48,745 --> 00:17:51,414
Whoever said that I'd be doing it alone?

361
00:17:58,004 --> 00:18:00,006
[wind whistling softly]

362
00:18:08,556 --> 00:18:09,390
Hmm?

363
00:18:11,267 --> 00:18:13,645
[dramatic music playing]

364
00:18:14,479 --> 00:18:16,147
[gasps] Mr. Yahya!

365
00:18:16,731 --> 00:18:18,399
I knew that you couldn't be dead!

366
00:18:18,983 --> 00:18:21,402
Oh? Were you terribly worried about me?

367
00:18:21,486 --> 00:18:22,987
[chuckles] Oh, your leg.

368
00:18:23,071 --> 00:18:25,990
I'm amazed you made it
into the fifth-floor window on that.

369
00:18:26,074 --> 00:18:29,202
Getting in wasn't a matter
of using my legs, but of using this.

370
00:18:29,285 --> 00:18:30,954
Oh, uh, cool.

371
00:18:31,037 --> 00:18:33,414
So, why are you in my apartment?

372
00:18:33,498 --> 00:18:36,918
Oh. What happened to you
pulling out your fangs?

373
00:18:37,001 --> 00:18:38,670
[splutters] Oh, these?

374
00:18:38,753 --> 00:18:41,840
Uh, they're just dentures.
I kind of need them to talk.

375
00:18:41,923 --> 00:18:45,176
Fangs for conversation, huh? How cute.

376
00:18:45,969 --> 00:18:48,054
I got you something. Know what it is?

377
00:18:48,138 --> 00:18:49,848
Whoa! Uh...

378
00:18:50,598 --> 00:18:51,641
A melon?

379
00:18:51,724 --> 00:18:53,726
- That's correct.
- [sniffs]

380
00:18:53,810 --> 00:18:56,855
But is that melon a vegetable,
or is it a fruit?

381
00:18:57,355 --> 00:18:59,232
Huh? Uh...

382
00:18:59,315 --> 00:19:01,568
Well, I mean,
a melon is a fruit, isn't it?

383
00:19:01,651 --> 00:19:04,112
But fruit tends to grow on trees,
does it not?

384
00:19:04,195 --> 00:19:05,488
Oh. That's true.

385
00:19:05,572 --> 00:19:07,448
So, a veggie?

386
00:19:07,532 --> 00:19:09,993
Perhaps. But do people eat vegetables
for dessert?

387
00:19:10,076 --> 00:19:13,037
Not typically.
So... [sighs] what is it? Mmm...

388
00:19:13,746 --> 00:19:16,249
Maybe it's a fruity sort of vegetable.

389
00:19:16,332 --> 00:19:20,211
[laughs] So you've come up with
a compromise, then.

390
00:19:20,295 --> 00:19:22,797
But, at the end of the day,
does it really matter?

391
00:19:23,798 --> 00:19:27,218
[Yahya] I've always hated it
when things aren't clear-cut.

392
00:19:27,886 --> 00:19:29,429
Like, for example,

393
00:19:29,512 --> 00:19:31,764
if a carnivore were
to pull out his own fangs,

394
00:19:31,848 --> 00:19:35,185
and claim that, through that act,
he became no different from an herbivore.

395
00:19:35,268 --> 00:19:37,312
Uh, is this payback for last time?

396
00:19:37,395 --> 00:19:40,064
Or if a child born
between a carnivore and herbivore

397
00:19:40,148 --> 00:19:41,900
exhibited traits of both.

398
00:19:43,443 --> 00:19:46,446
And that is the case
for the criminal I'm pursuing right now.

399
00:19:46,529 --> 00:19:49,157
An unnatural mix
of carnivore and herbivore.

400
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,116
They're a mix?

401
00:19:50,617 --> 00:19:53,828
That's right. And the name
of this culprit is Melon.

402
00:19:53,912 --> 00:19:55,580
Oh. What did he do?

403
00:19:56,164 --> 00:19:59,918
He pretends to be an herbivore
to draw in other herbivores.

404
00:20:00,001 --> 00:20:02,837
He befriends them, makes them feel safe,
then he strikes!

405
00:20:02,921 --> 00:20:05,506
[yelps] What a horrifying devourer.

406
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:08,301
Wrong. He doesn't devour them.

407
00:20:08,384 --> 00:20:09,469
What?

408
00:20:09,552 --> 00:20:12,222
He's killed his fair share,
but hasn't eaten anyone.

409
00:20:12,305 --> 00:20:14,349
He kills because he enjoys it.

410
00:20:15,642 --> 00:20:18,603
More devious than your average devourer,
wouldn't you say?

411
00:20:19,479 --> 00:20:21,147
Why would someone do that?

412
00:20:21,231 --> 00:20:24,651
Indeed. We'll never find out
unless we ask.

413
00:20:24,734 --> 00:20:27,904
If he is out there, why are you
wasting your time talking to me?

414
00:20:27,987 --> 00:20:31,157
- Go out and catch this guy!
- Ordinarily, I'd be happy to.

415
00:20:31,824 --> 00:20:35,245
But to a horse, a leg injury
can be one hell of a problem.

416
00:20:35,328 --> 00:20:36,246
Oh, right.

417
00:20:37,413 --> 00:20:39,874
So, will you help me bring him down?

418
00:20:39,958 --> 00:20:42,377
Help me arrest Melon,
the cruel mixed beast.

419
00:20:43,294 --> 00:20:44,671
[hesitates] Uh...

420
00:20:44,754 --> 00:20:48,466
I understand. It's an exceptionally
dangerous task.

421
00:20:48,549 --> 00:20:51,678
But it won't be unpaid.
I can offer you ten million.

422
00:20:52,345 --> 00:20:53,429
Huh?

423
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,640
Is this some sort of a prank?

424
00:20:55,723 --> 00:20:57,350
I don't need that kind of money!

425
00:20:57,433 --> 00:21:00,853
I'm happy living here, working at
the udon restaurant. That's enough for me.

426
00:21:00,937 --> 00:21:02,689
Yes, but,

427
00:21:02,772 --> 00:21:06,359
someday you might want to build
a modest home with a cute little bunny.

428
00:21:06,442 --> 00:21:09,487
- Wouldn't it be nice to have the funds?
- [gasps] Just leave me alone!

429
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:12,532
Why even bring this to me?
Is it bitterness?

430
00:21:12,615 --> 00:21:14,367
Is it because I'm Gosha's grandson?

431
00:21:14,951 --> 00:21:15,785
Oh.

432
00:21:16,327 --> 00:21:17,704
Oh, no.

433
00:21:17,787 --> 00:21:22,000
I simply thought you might appreciate
a little glimpse into your own future.

434
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:23,001
Huh?

435
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:27,630
A cautionary tale of love
between an herbivore and carnivore

436
00:21:27,714 --> 00:21:31,676
told through the twisted, broken creature
their coupling brought forth.

437
00:21:32,885 --> 00:21:35,805
[Legoshi] <i>A child,
like Haru and I could have.</i>

438
00:21:35,888 --> 00:21:38,141
[tense music playing]

439
00:21:49,319 --> 00:21:51,696
- [Yahya] Well, Legoshi?
- [gasps softly]

440
00:21:57,076 --> 00:21:59,287
[music fades]

441
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

442
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,834
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

443
00:22:04,917 --> 00:22:08,254
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

444
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,467
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

445
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,678
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

446
00:22:17,805 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

447
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,561
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

448
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

449
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,569
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

450
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

451
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

452
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,832
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

453
00:22:44,916 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

454
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,044
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

455
00:22:48,127 --> 00:22:52,548
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

456
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

457
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,807
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

458
00:23:00,890 --> 00:23:02,767
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

459
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,143
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

460
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:08,731
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my sid</i> e ♪

461
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,608
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

462
00:23:10,691 --> 00:23:12,652
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

463
00:23:13,402 --> 00:23:16,364
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

464
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

465
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,372
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

466
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:28,793
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
